From: MedyMa <MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: add exclusive native TOPS flowtable provider

Add typed, RCU protected leases for the optional NETSYSv3 native PPE
backend. Only supported plain IPv4 PPTP/L2TP paths enter this backend;
unsupported encapsulation remains on the software path. Keep inner
software packets away from direct physical transmit, retain tunnel owner
identity in both directions, and drain packet accounting on retirement.
Quiesce PPP channel close and peer driven L2TP framing changes before
reusing hardware state. Vendor HNAT remains a separate exclusive mode.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -56,4 +56,14 @@
 	  in the MediaTek MT7988/MT7986/MT2701/MT7622/MT7629/MT7621 chipset
 	  family.
 
+config NET_MEDIATEK_NPU_FLOW
+	bool "MediaTek NPU support for native Linux flowtables"
+	depends on NET_MEDIATEK_SOC && NF_FLOW_TABLE && INET && PPP
+	select MTK_PPP_TUNNEL_INFO
+	depends on MEDIATEK_NETSYS_V3 && NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT=n
+	default n
+	help
+	  Use the native PPE flowtable driver as the owner of NPU tunnel actions.
+	  Vendor HNAT uses the same PPE tables and cannot be enabled together.
+
 endif #NET_VENDOR_MEDIATEK
